# [DD-13b.W1.3] Q-W2 (D89 point 3): `(?R)` INSIDE A BOUND DEFINITION IS
# REFUSED. After injection it could mean the caller's whole pattern or the
# definition's own body, and D89 chose mechanisms over silent defaults — the
# refusal says the RULING is missing, not the meaning.
#
# It is raised at the SUB-PARSE, because nothing later can tell it from the
# three other situations that leave `u.call.target` at 0 (the arena zero, a
# deferred cross-definition call, and a call the composer has not reached).
target = caller

pattern ^(?&selfy)$
name caller

pattern a(?R)?b
name selfy
